## BASE AGENT CLIENTS
BaseAgent initializes these LLM clients available to every agent:
  self.groq      — AsyncGroq (groq library) — for Llama 3.1 70B + Qwen 72B
  self.gemini    — google.generativeai (google-generativeai library) — for Gemini Flash + Pro
  self.deepseek  — AsyncOpenAI with base_url="https://api.deepseek.com" — for DeepSeek backup
  self.anthropic — AsyncAnthropic (optional, demo only)

When generating BaseAgent or any agent code, always include
the Gemini client using google.generativeai library.
Use the ASYNC version — never the sync version:
  import google.generativeai as genai
  genai.configure(api_key=get_next_key(GEMINI_KEYS, attempt))
  model = genai.GenerativeModel(LLMModel.GEMINI_FLASH)
  response = await model.generate_content_async(prompt)
  result = response.text

Never use model.generate_content() (sync) — always generate_content_async().

## AGENT COMMUNICATION PATTERN
Agents communicate ONLY through:
1. LangGraph state object — for workflow state and phase transitions
2. ChromaDB — for all knowledge, attack history, and results
NEVER pass data between agents directly as function arguments.
NEVER use global variables to share state between agents.

## CHROMADB RULES
Every query to ChromaDB MUST include client_id filter:
  collection.query(where={"client_id": client_id}, ...)
Every record stored MUST include client_id in metadata.
This is a hard security rule. No exceptions. Ever.
Collections: attack_history, successful_attacks, mutation_lineage,
             component_profiles, vulnerability_catalog

## WEBSOCKET EVENTS
All backend events broadcast as JSON with fields:
  scan_id, timestamp, event_type (from WSEvent constants)
Event types: agent_started, attack_executed, mutation_occurred,
             vulnerability_found, component_complete, scan_complete,
             critical_halt, progress_update
Frontend Zustand store handles each event type with a dedicated action.

## SECURITY RULES — NON-NEGOTIABLE
1. Every scan requires a valid consent_id in PostgreSQL before starting
2. No attack executes without scan status = ACTIVE in database
3. All ChromaDB queries filter by client_id — zero exceptions
4. AutopatchAgent checks approved_findings list before every single patch
5. Client credentials stored encrypted — never plain text
6. .env file never committed to GitHub under any circumstances
7. API keys never typed into any chat, Discord, WhatsApp, or Notion

## SCORE TO ACTION MAPPING
0.0 - 0.09: No effect — log and continue
0.1 - 0.39: Low — log, low priority mutation
0.4 - 0.69: Medium — feed to MutationAgent
0.7 - 0.89: High — flag as vulnerability, continue scan
0.9 - 1.0:  CRITICAL — halt scan immediately, alert client, broadcast WSEvent.CRITICAL_HALT
